"with :c:type:`SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU` or **ctor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:321
msgid ""
"By default, :c:type:`SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU` and **ctor** caches place the "
"free pointer outside of the object. This might cause the object to grow in "
"size. Cache creators that have a reason to avoid this can specify a custom "
"free pointer offset in their data structure where the free pointer will be "
"placed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:327
msgid ""
"For caches with :c:type:`SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU`, the caller must ensure that "
"the free pointer does not overlay fields required to guard against object "
"recycling (See :c:type:`SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU` for details)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:331
msgid ""
"For caches with **ctor**, the caller must ensure that the free pointer does "
"not overlay fields initialized by the constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:334
msgid ""
"Currently, only caches with :c:type:`SLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU` or **ctor** may "
"specify **freeptr_offset**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:337
msgid ""
"Using ``0`` as a value for **freeptr_offset** is valid. If "
"**freeptr_offset** is specified, **use_freeptr_offset** must be set ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:341
msgid "``use_freeptr_offset``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:40: ../include/linux/slab.h:342
