msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:137: ../mm/migrate_device.c:1406
msgid ""
"This is useful when a driver needs to free device memory but doesn't know "
"the virtual mappings of every page that may be in device memory. For example "
"this is often the case when a driver is being unloaded or unbound from a "
"device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:137: ../mm/migrate_device.c:1410
msgid ""
"Like migrate_vma_setup() this function will take a reference and lock any "
"migrating pages that aren't free before unmapping them. Drivers may then "
"allocate destination pages and start copying data from the device to CPU "
"memory before calling migrate_device_pages()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:137: ../mm/migrate_device.c:1454
msgid "pre-populated array of source device private pfns to migrate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:137: ../mm/migrate_device.c:1456
