msgid "``struct page *lock_at``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4284
msgid "a page within **folio** to be left locked to caller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4285
msgid "after-split folios will be put on it if non NULL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4286
msgid "perform uniform split or not (non-uniform split)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4287
msgid ""
"It calls __split_frozen_folio() to perform uniform and non-uniform split. It "
"is in charge of checking whether the split is supported or not and preparing "
"**folio** for __split_frozen_folio()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4291
msgid ""
"After splitting, the after-split folio containing **lock_at** remains locked "
"and others are unlocked: 1. for uniform split, **lock_at** points to one of "
"**folio**'s subpages; 2. for buddy allocator like (non-uniform) split, "
"**lock_at** points to **folio**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4366
msgid "split a large anon folio that is already unmapped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:147: ../mm/huge_memory.c:4368
